// Editorial dossiers: primary-source research checked 24 October 2026.
// Prices describe the named billing period and exclude tax and Meta delivery fees unless stated.
export const providers = [];
const p = (slug, name, category, url, profile, pricing, scenario, advantage, fit) => providers.push({ slug: `whatflow-vs-${slug}`, name, category, url, profile, pricing, scenario, advantage, fit });
p('wati','Wati','whatsapp','https://www.wati.io/en/pricing/',
'Wati offers a WhatsApp sales and support platform with a Shopify connector. Its documented ecommerce workflows include cart recovery, COD confirmation, shipping updates and catalog experiences. This is a real Shopify competitor, so the comparison should begin with the work an operator can complete, rather than whether an integration exists.',
'Wati lists different included-user allowances across its plans and paid additional users on eligible tiers. Its Shopify integration guide also describes a separate plugin charge. Request a quote that identifies the plan, Shopify connector, user allowance and message charges together; do not compare the subscription alone with an all-inclusive application.',
'A store adds warehouse staff to help with COD replies during a promotion. Evaluate the bill before and after those colleagues join, then inspect how a confirmation is recorded against the Shopify order.',
'WhatFlow keeps the inbox accessible without seat charges and makes every feature available on every plan. The plan decision is about sending volume, rather than whether order automation or another colleague deserves an upgrade.',
'Wati can suit a wider WhatsApp sales organization that values its broader platform and is comfortable with the quoted plan and connector terms.');
p('interakt','Interakt','shopify','https://www.interakt.shop/integrations/integrating-whatsapp-business-api-with-shopify/',
'Interakt advertises Shopify commerce journeys, catalog synchronization, segmented messaging and COD-to-prepaid use cases. Its materials also discuss voice-assisted journeys. A merchant comparing it with WhatFlow should distinguish useful WhatsApp order operations from the extra selling capabilities they might eventually want.',
'Interakt’s Shopify page displays monthly options at $41, $51 and $99. Treat those as the advertised software options for that page, then confirm messaging fees, taxes and any required add-ons. WhatFlow Starter is $4.99 per month with 2,000 included sends; those subscription figures are comparable only after the required functionality and usage are aligned.',
'A COD shopper replies asking to change the address and pay online instead. Follow the reply through the inbox and inspect the Shopify order before allowing fulfillment.',
'WhatFlow offers Shopify extensions, order-linked automation and a team inbox without moving feature access into a higher subscription. That makes it a compelling first choice when the store needs the operational journey more than a separate sales platform.',
'Interakt deserves a look when its additional commerce or voice scope is central to the rollout, rather than an attractive demonstration you are unlikely to use.');
p('bitespeed','BiteSpeed','shopify','https://www.bitespeed.co/',
'BiteSpeed positions itself across ecommerce marketing, sales and support, including WhatsApp, email, SMS, voice and social channels. Its breadth can matter to a retention team coordinating several campaigns. It also makes the buying decision larger than choosing an app to send Shopify order updates.',
'Use an itemized BiteSpeed proposal rather than an assumed entry price. Specify the channels, contacts, messages, agents and services you actually need. A quote for a cross-channel platform is not evidence of what a WhatsApp-only deployment costs, and an unpublished quote is not a defensible basis for a percentage-savings claim.',
'A founder already has email working well and wants to add WhatsApp cart reminders. Compare the cost of adding the missing channel with the cost and work of moving the entire retention stack.',
'WhatFlow lets the store keep its existing email setup while adding Shopify-connected WhatsApp, a no-seat-fee inbox and the full feature set from the free plan upward.',
'BiteSpeed may be the better organizational fit when consolidating marketing channels is itself the project and the team will actively use that breadth.');
p('quickreply','QuickReply.ai','shopify','https://docs.quickreply.ai/',
'QuickReply.ai documents Shopify journeys and ecommerce automations. It should be evaluated as an ecommerce messaging product, not dismissed as a generic chatbot. The useful distinction is how its journey tooling, commercial terms and everyday operating process compare with WhatFlow’s Shopify-first approach.',
'Confirm the current plan and messaging terms directly with QuickReply.ai. Ask whether the quoted package includes the journeys, support access, users and reporting shown in the demo. An attractive headline becomes less useful if the workflow you actually want belongs to another package.',
'Build a cart reminder with a delay, then complete checkout before the delay expires. Review how the selected journey handles that completed order and whether an operator can investigate it without developer assistance.',
'WhatFlow’s all-features policy removes the need to choose a subscription based on access to one particular automation. The store can select its message allowance and keep the same inbox and Shopify feature access.',
'QuickReply.ai is worth considering for teams that prefer its journey-building approach and receive a package that fits their actual send mix.');
p('aisensy','AiSensy','shopify','https://aisensy.com/integrations/shopify',
'AiSensy offers WhatsApp campaigns and Shopify integrations, including ecommerce automation and dynamic message content. Merchants should compare the actual integration path and package instead of assuming that only WhatFlow understands store events.',
'Get the relevant AiSensy country pricing and the exact plan used for Shopify automation. Separate software fees from Meta delivery charges and optional services. Local-currency subscription prices need a stated currency and billing term before they can support a fair comparison.',
'A merchant changes a product image and updates an abandoned checkout template. Check how product details map into the message and how the operations team handles the customer’s resulting question.',
'WhatFlow’s advantage is the combination of Shopify-native working surfaces, complete feature access and an inbox that does not introduce a per-person subscription as the team expands.',
'AiSensy can work for teams that prioritize its wider WhatsApp campaign ecosystem and the available local commercial package.');
p('zoko','Zoko','shopify','https://www.zoko.io/',
'Zoko focuses on WhatsApp commerce for Shopify, with catalog-led selling, a shared inbox and automation flows. That is close enough to WhatFlow’s audience that a broad feature checklist will not decide the purchase. Look at pricing structure and the route from a reply to a usable Shopify outcome.',
'Ask Zoko for the current subscription, usage model, included users and automation allowances. Keep any WhatsApp charges visible. Do not assume that a particular package includes every module merely because the product site advertises it.',
'A buyer asks about a product, places a COD order and then confirms it in the same conversation. Work through the selling step, the confirmation and the order record rather than stopping at a delivered template.',
'WhatFlow makes its team inbox and Shopify capabilities available across plans with no seat fees. For a store that values simple operating costs, that is a concrete reason to start the evaluation here.',
'Zoko can appeal to teams whose buying priority is its particular conversational commerce experience and who will use the quoted catalog and selling tools.');
p('delightchat','DelightChat','shopify','https://www.delightchat.io/',
'DelightChat combines ecommerce customer support with WhatsApp marketing and automation. It publishes WhatsApp integration guidance and Shopify Flow material. Its appeal is the overlap between support conversations and retention activity, so compare both responsibilities if you intend to consolidate them.',
'Request a package covering the support volume, WhatsApp messages, users and automation requirements you expect. Distinguish helpdesk consumption from WhatsApp delivery fees. A support package may be good value for a busy helpdesk while still being more than a store needs for a focused WhatsApp rollout.',
'A delivery question reaches the inbox after an automated fulfillment message. Ask the support operator to identify the order, reply and hand over the conversation at the end of a shift.',
'WhatFlow gives the store an included team inbox alongside Shopify order automation, without charging each additional colleague. It is especially attractive when the missing piece is WhatsApp rather than a new multichannel support system.',
'DelightChat is relevant when the team wants its broader ecommerce helpdesk to become the main home for support.');
p('klaviyo','Klaviyo','shopify','https://www.klaviyo.com/products/whatsapp',
'Klaviyo now offers WhatsApp as part of its customer engagement ecosystem. Comparing WhatFlow with an outdated description of Klaviyo as email-only would be misleading. Its case is unified customer data and coordinated marketing across channels.',
'Klaviyo pricing depends on the selected products, audience and usage. Obtain a quote that includes WhatsApp for the relevant countries and message categories. Do not use a free email allowance as though it were a free WhatsApp package, or assume an email subscription automatically includes the desired WhatsApp sends.',
'A shopper receives an email campaign and a WhatsApp checkout reminder before buying. Agree which system owns suppression, audience updates and attribution, so the same order does not become two separate revenue claims.',
'WhatFlow offers a practical way to add WhatsApp operations without replacing the store’s existing email platform. The free-forever storefront button, no-seat-fee inbox and all-features plans help keep that addition affordable.',
'Klaviyo can be a strong fit when a dedicated lifecycle team needs its unified data and cross-channel orchestration rather than a focused Shopify WhatsApp app.');
p('tidio','Tidio','support','https://www.tidio.com/',
'Tidio combines a helpdesk, live chat, automation and Lyro AI, and advertises WhatsApp support within its channel offering. Its strongest comparison with WhatFlow is how a store wants to handle service, rather than a simplistic contest over whether either product has a chat bubble.',
'Price the helpdesk and AI components separately where applicable. Confirm the plan needed for WhatsApp and the AI usage included in that package. An AI conversation allowance is a different billing unit from a sent WhatsApp message.',
'A customer asks a product question from the storefront and later follows up about shipping. Decide whether your first priority is an AI-led site support experience or a Shopify-linked WhatsApp conversation with human ownership.',
'WhatFlow keeps the inbox, theme-matched WhatsApp button and Shopify automation within the same feature-access policy. The budget grows with the messaging plan instead of a seat count.',
'Tidio merits attention when Lyro and website support automation are the main purchase, with WhatsApp as one part of that broader service design.');
p('gorgias','Gorgias','support','https://helpcenter.gorgias.com/en-US/handle-tickets-in-gorgias-whatsapp-8200191',
'Gorgias is an ecommerce helpdesk with WhatsApp support, including template-based outbound initiation in its current documentation. WhatsApp interactions can become billable tickets under the documented conditions. It is not accurate to claim that Gorgias is incapable of proactive WhatsApp messaging.',
'Calculate the helpdesk bill using the applicable ticket definition, not just agent count. Gorgias documents that a WhatsApp ticket becomes billable when it receives a public reply. Add the relevant messaging fees and any selected AI or service components to estimate the actual workload.',
'A store sends tracking updates and receives many short “thank you” replies alongside genuine delivery problems. Apply the vendor’s billing definition to the replies and the public responses before comparing totals.',
'WhatFlow’s included inbox and message-based plans are easy to understand for a merchant buying WhatsApp operations. There is no additional seat subscription to add the colleague who handles delivery exceptions.',
'Gorgias may still be the right central helpdesk for a team with substantial ticket management needs across channels. That does not mean every Shopify store needs a full helpdesk purchase to start WhatsApp.');
p('limechat','LimeChat','shopify','https://www.limechat.ai/',
'LimeChat emphasizes AI-powered commerce, customer experience and voice alongside WhatsApp. That enterprise-oriented scope deserves a different evaluation from a lightweight order messaging app. Ask which outcomes require implementation services or AI configuration before comparing the demo with a self-serve workflow.',
'Use a current LimeChat quote covering the required channels, AI usage and implementation. Without a public like-for-like package, a precise savings percentage would be speculation. WhatFlow’s published message allowances give a store an accessible baseline while it evaluates whether the additional AI scope is necessary.',
'A brand wants an AI agent to answer product questions before a human handles an exception. Map the handoff, source of product information and ownership of incorrect answers before expanding the automation.',
'For merchants who want to begin with Shopify events and a human team inbox, WhatFlow offers a more straightforward purchasing decision: every feature is available, users do not carry seat fees, and plans scale by messages.',
'LimeChat can make sense where an AI-led commerce initiative has a defined budget, owner and implementation plan.');
p('chatarmin','Chatarmin','shopify','https://chatarmin.com/en/',
'Chatarmin markets WhatsApp for ecommerce, including Shopify integrations and marketing or service workflows. A merchant should compare the package and daily workflow rather than assuming that a European-focused platform is interchangeable with an app installed primarily for Shopify operations.',
'Ask for the subscription, messaging charges, required onboarding and any plan-specific features in the current proposal. If the quote is in euros, retain that currency in the comparison instead of silently mixing it with WhatFlow’s US-dollar listing.',
'A retention manager launches a segmented promotion while support handles order questions from the same customer group. Review who maintains the segments and how the team avoids treating a support reply as permission for unrelated promotions.',
'WhatFlow makes the team inbox and Shopify feature set available even on the free plan. That keeps a smaller merchant from paying for a higher software package simply to use another part of the app.',
'Chatarmin can appeal to ecommerce teams seeking its particular regional offering and marketing workflow, provided the quote matches the intended rollout.');
p('charles','charles','shopify','https://www.hello-charles.com/',
'charles presents a conversational commerce platform for customer acquisition, lifecycle marketing and service on WhatsApp. Its enterprise approach may include substantial strategic and operational work around campaigns. That scope should be explicit when comparing it with a Shopify application.',
'Use the actual charles proposal, including services and implementation, rather than attributing an invented public price. A store should decide whether it needs the services attached to an enterprise program before comparing the software invoice alone.',
'A brand plans a major WhatsApp acquisition campaign and expects specialists to design the journey. Separate the value of those services from the cost of sending Shopify order messages and answering customers.',
'WhatFlow is a strong starting point for a store that wants to own its WhatsApp workflows directly inside its Shopify operation. No feature gates or seat fees are required to access that foundation.',
'charles may fit a larger brand funding a broader conversational commerce program, especially when the surrounding expertise is part of what it wants to buy.');
p('superlemon','SuperLemon','shopify','https://superlemon.xyz/',
'SuperLemon is associated with Shopify WhatsApp buttons, abandoned checkout recovery, order updates and broadcasts. Compare the free widget offering separately from automation subscriptions; a storefront shortcut and a managed messaging workflow solve different problems.',
'Confirm the current SuperLemon plan for each required function rather than treating the presence of a free widget as free automated sending. For WhatFlow, the theme-matched button is free forever while automated message usage follows the selected allowance and applicable delivery charges.',
'A merchant initially installs a WhatsApp button and later needs COD replies, checkout reminders and a shared inbox. Price that second stage before choosing solely on the appearance of the first widget.',
'WhatFlow’s appeal is continuity: the free button belongs to the same Shopify-focused app as the inbox and automation, and feature access does not change when the merchant selects a different message plan.',
'SuperLemon is worth testing when its particular widget or automation experience matches the store’s requirements and current package.');
p('respond-io','respond.io','whatsapp','https://respond.io/pricing',
'respond.io is a conversation platform spanning channels, automation and customer-facing teams. Its pricing combines plan scope, included users and monthly active contacts. Those units reflect a broader operating model than simply counting a Shopify store’s outbound messages.',
'The pricing page lists included-user allowances of five or ten depending on plan, with additional-user charges displayed at $12, $20 or $24 per month for the relevant tiers. Confirm the active-contact allowance and WhatsApp charges too. Avoid comparing only the price of an extra user with the cost of an entire application.',
'A sales organization wants lead routing across several channels, while the store team mainly needs shipping and cart conversations. Identify which responsibility is driving the purchase before paying for the larger operating model.',
'WhatFlow has no seat fees and does not gate its Shopify features by plan. A store can invite the people who actually handle orders without turning each handoff into another recurring user charge.',
'respond.io can be a good fit when the business genuinely needs its broader conversation operations and contact-based planning.');
p('manychat','Manychat','whatsapp','https://manychat.com/product/whatsapp',
'Manychat offers social and WhatsApp automation for acquisition, follow-up and customer conversations. Its WhatsApp materials include broadcasts, welcome flows and automated responses. The distinction for a Shopify merchant is whether the central job is social lead conversion or store operations.',
'Confirm the current Manychat package, contact limits and WhatsApp wallet or delivery charges for the account and region. Do not assume that a social automation free tier provides unlimited WhatsApp business messaging.',
'A creator sends social followers into a conversation and then into a Shopify checkout. Decide which system owns the lead before purchase and which owns the order after purchase; those may be complementary jobs.',
'WhatFlow is built around Shopify order and checkout context, with an included inbox and feature access independent of plan. That makes it an appealing home for the operational part of the customer relationship.',
'Manychat may be the better acquisition tool when social conversation funnels are the main project; it can coexist with a Shopify-focused operations app.');
p('twilio','Twilio','api','https://www.twilio.com/en-us/whatsapp/pricing',
'Twilio provides programmable WhatsApp messaging rather than a ready-made Shopify operating workflow. Developers can build deeply customized experiences with it, but a messaging endpoint does not automatically supply an order-linked inbox, a theme extension or a maintained Shopify event integration.',
'Twilio lists a $0.005 platform fee for each inbound or outbound WhatsApp message, with Meta template fees additional. For 5,000 outbound messages and no inbound traffic in the example, that is $25 in Twilio platform fees. WhatFlow Plus is $9.99 including 5,000 sends. This comparison excludes Meta fees on both sides and excludes engineering or additional Twilio products; inbound replies would change the Twilio calculation.',
'A developer connects an order webhook, then must add retry handling, template variables, delivery status storage and a way for support staff to reply. Scope that complete system before calling the API route the cheaper option.',
'WhatFlow packages Shopify integration, a team inbox and the complete feature set with its message plan. For a merchant, the time saved maintaining that application can matter as much as the platform-fee difference.',
'Twilio remains a strong option when the business needs a custom multi-system communications product and has engineers responsible for its ongoing operation.');
p('360dialog','360dialog','api','https://360dialog.com/',
'360dialog supplies WhatsApp Business Platform infrastructure and works with an ecosystem of partners. It is useful to distinguish the channel or number service from the application a merchant will use for automation and customer replies.',
'Include the relevant 360dialog license or channel charge, the selected inbox or partner application, implementation and Meta fees. A statement about no markup on Meta charges does not imply that the entire operational stack is free.',
'A store buys channel access and then realizes that staff still need an inbox and an order integration. Obtain the complete partner proposal before comparing it with an application that already includes those working surfaces.',
'WhatFlow brings the Shopify workflow and team inbox into one app and does not introduce per-seat subscription fees. Its all-features approach reduces the number of separate purchases needed to get started.',
'360dialog can fit developers or partners who deliberately want to assemble a WhatsApp stack around their preferred applications.');
p('gallabox','Gallabox','whatsapp','https://gallabox.com/',
'Gallabox emphasizes lead capture, qualification, automation and conversational selling across WhatsApp and other channels. Its product breadth can help sales teams, while a Shopify merchant may be primarily concerned with order events and customer support after checkout.',
'Request a package specifying users, automation, integrations and messaging fees. Confirm whether the sales features in the demonstration are included in the quoted subscription. Plan entitlement is more useful than a long undifferentiated feature list.',
'A business captures enquiries before a purchase and passes them to a sales representative. Compare that lead process separately from the Shopify order-confirmation process so that one does not hide gaps in the other.',
'WhatFlow is attractive when Shopify is already the operational center: it offers store-linked messaging, a team inbox without seat charges and full feature access even at entry level.',
'Gallabox may suit a team that is deliberately buying lead qualification and conversational sales operations across channels.');
p('doubletick','DoubleTick','whatsapp','https://doubletick.io/',
'DoubleTick markets WhatsApp for sales teams, including shared conversations, automation and organizational controls. Its audience can include businesses coordinating representatives and departments beyond a single ecommerce store.',
'Ask for the current price with the intended team structure, numbers, automation and usage. A sales-team quotation should identify exactly which capabilities and allowances are included; avoid assuming public feature descriptions establish a universal price.',
'A business has several departments answering the same audience. Map number ownership, conversation handoffs and where the final customer or order record lives before choosing the inbox.',
'For a Shopify-led team, WhatFlow offers a simpler anchor: the store’s own events and order context, combined with a no-seat-fee inbox and all-features plans.',
'DoubleTick deserves consideration when its wider sales organization model is a requirement rather than an optional extra.');
p('gupshup','Gupshup','api','https://www.gupshup.ai/',
'Gupshup provides conversational engagement technology, including WhatsApp infrastructure, automation and AI or voice-oriented offerings. A merchant should identify the exact product and implementation partner in the proposal; a large provider’s portfolio is not a single standardized Shopify application.',
'Price the chosen product, channel usage, implementation and operational application. Public claims about channel reach or scale do not tell you what the store’s inbox, integration or support package will cost.',
'A larger company wants WhatsApp connected to several systems and perhaps voice journeys. Draw the system boundaries and identify who maintains each integration when a Shopify order changes.',
'WhatFlow is a compelling alternative for the store that wants those Shopify workflows already packaged, with no feature gates or seat-based inbox subscription.',
'Gupshup may be appropriate for a broader conversational infrastructure project with dedicated technical ownership and a clear implementation scope.');
p('infobip','Infobip','api','https://www.infobip.com/whatsapp-business',
'Infobip offers WhatsApp within a broad communications and customer engagement portfolio. That scope can be valuable to enterprises coordinating channels, applications and markets. It also means a useful comparison must identify the particular products being proposed.',
'Obtain an itemized quote covering WhatsApp delivery, the operational inbox or engagement product, implementation and support. A channel rate alone is not the price of a Shopify-ready messaging operation.',
'A multinational team wants central communications infrastructure while a store operator needs to edit an order template. Show how that everyday change moves through the proposed system and who is responsible for deploying it.',
'WhatFlow keeps Shopify template work close to the merchant and includes the team inbox without a seat bill. Every plan provides feature access, so the merchant can start small without buying an enterprise implementation.',
'Infobip can fit organizations with enterprise procurement and cross-channel infrastructure requirements beyond the store.');
p('bird','Bird','api','https://bird.com/whatsapp-api/features/marketing',
'Bird offers WhatsApp marketing and customer engagement within a broader messaging platform. Its current materials cover campaign and template-related workflows. Compare the specific Bird application and usage model, rather than an old MessageBird product description.',
'Ask for the selected Bird package, audience or usage basis, WhatsApp charges and implementation costs. Distinguish a messaging API quote from a complete campaign and inbox deployment.',
'A marketing team wants unified audience operations while store staff need quick access to order-linked replies. Give each group a concrete task and check whether the same purchase actually supports both.',
'WhatFlow is easy to justify for the Shopify operational layer: no seat fees, no feature gates and published message plans, alongside a free-forever theme-matched button.',
'Bird may fit a broader engagement platform project where its channel and audience capabilities will be used consistently.');
p('whatsapp-business-app','WhatsApp Business app','whatsapp','https://business.whatsapp.com/products/business-app',
'The WhatsApp Business app is an accessible way for a small business to start customer conversations. Its catalog and everyday messaging tools are useful, and eligible businesses may also see newer AI features. Do not confuse the free app with a Shopify event automation system or assume every business receives the same rollout.',
'The app’s free entry point is a real advantage. The comparison is the work surrounding a message: finding the order, selecting the correct details, handling repeated updates and coordinating staff. WhatFlow also has a free plan and a free-forever storefront button, while automated sends follow the selected allowance and delivery rules.',
'A founder copies order details into individual chats every evening. That can work at first, but a missed fulfillment update or an unanswered reply exposes the limits of a process that depends entirely on someone remembering the next step.',
'WhatFlow adds Shopify-triggered messages, mapped store data and an included team inbox without per-seat fees. It turns repeatable store events into a maintained workflow while keeping humans available for the exceptions.',
'The Business app can remain the right choice for a very small, largely manual operation; check number eligibility and migration or coexistence options before changing a live setup.');
p('sleekflow','SleekFlow','whatsapp','https://sleekflow.io/pricing',
'SleekFlow combines an omnichannel inbox, automated flows and conversational commerce tools. Its pricing materials also describe CRM, analytics and service capabilities. That breadth is useful to teams organizing customer communication across departments; it also calls for a more detailed scope than simply adding WhatsApp to Shopify.',
'Confirm the regional price, included users, contacts and automation allowances for the selected package. Include WhatsApp delivery costs and any commerce or AI components required for the proposed workflow. Regional pricing should retain its original currency and billing period.',
'A retailer has online staff, a physical sales team and a centralized service desk. Test how ownership passes between those groups, and whether a Shopify operator can still investigate a failed order update without waiting for another department.',
'WhatFlow is an appealing choice for the Shopify portion of that work because its inbox has no seat fees and its plans preserve full feature access at every volume.',
'SleekFlow can be useful when the organization wants a broader conversation platform and will use its cross-department tooling.');
p('trengo','Trengo','support','https://trengo.com/prices',
'Trengo is a multichannel customer conversation platform with team collaboration and automation. It sells bundled software packages rather than a simple charge for each WhatsApp send. This matters when a merchant with a small support team compares the minimum monthly commitment.',
'Trengo displays Boost at €349 month to month, including ten users and 500 conversations per month. Its annual option shows a lower monthly equivalent with an annual conversation allowance. Those are different commercial commitments. Compare the month-to-month floor with WhatFlow’s US-dollar plans without silently converting currencies or assuming all conversation and message units are equivalent.',
'A three-person store needs a shared WhatsApp inbox but does not need ten user places. Work out whether the bundled package is still valuable when much of its included team capacity is unused.',
'WhatFlow allows a team to choose a messaging allowance rather than a bundled user package, while retaining all features and paying no seat fees.',
'Trengo can be sensible for a larger multichannel support operation that will use the included users and broader service tooling.');
p('timelinesai','TimelinesAI','support','https://timelines.ai/timelinesai-pricing',
'TimelinesAI connects WhatsApp communication with sales CRMs such as HubSpot, Pipedrive and Salesforce. Its offering includes shared conversations and automation, with connection options that should be checked for the chosen account. Its natural center of gravity is a sales pipeline rather than a Shopify order.',
'TimelinesAI displays Starter at $35 per seat per month and Pro at $49. Five Starter seats therefore cost $175 per month before any separately applicable services or delivery charges. Automation credits also vary by package. This is a seat-subscription example, not a complete delivery-cost comparison.',
'A sales manager wants every chat reflected in a deal record, while fulfillment staff want each reply tied to an order. Decide which record drives the business process before choosing the integration.',
'WhatFlow’s no-seat-fee inbox gives Shopify support and operations staff access without multiplying a $35 user subscription. Its plans change messaging allowances, not access to the app’s features.',
'TimelinesAI can be a strong fit when the sales CRM is the primary record and WhatsApp synchronization there is the central requirement.');
p('kommo','Kommo','support','https://www.kommo.com/buy/tariff/',
'Kommo is a sales CRM with messaging and automation around leads and pipelines. A store may find that useful for assisted selling, especially when opportunities need follow-up before an order exists. It is a different purchasing priority from responding to Shopify events after checkout.',
'Kommo’s current pricing starts at $25 per user per month for Base, with Advanced at $35 and Pro at $45; check the required subscription term. Five Base users produce a $125 monthly equivalent before messaging or integration extras. Do not reuse older $15 entry-price comparisons.',
'A wholesale enquiry needs a quotation, a salesperson and several follow-ups before purchase. Compare that lead pipeline separately from confirmations, shipping updates and customer questions once Shopify holds the order.',
'WhatFlow is economical for the store operations layer: a shared inbox without seat charges and complete feature access, with spending determined by the selected message plan.',
'Kommo may be preferable when a structured sales pipeline is the missing business system; WhatFlow does not need to replace that CRM to handle Shopify WhatsApp workflows.');
p('freshchat','Freshchat','support','https://www.freshworks.com/live-chat-software/pricing/',
'Freshchat provides customer messaging within the Freshworks ecosystem, with helpdesk and AI-related options depending on the package. Its free plan for up to ten agents is important context; a fair comparison cannot pretend that every additional person always creates a paid Freshchat seat.',
'The pricing page lists paid Growth at $19 per agent per month billed annually, with higher tiers and separate AI options. Five Growth agents correspond to $95 per month on that annual billing basis. Confirm the package that includes the desired WhatsApp channel; the free widget plan is not automatically the same configuration.',
'A support manager wants a broader messaging desk and AI assistance. List the channels and automations actually required before assuming the free tier or the first paid tier covers the intended service design.',
'WhatFlow keeps its inbox and Shopify capabilities available across plans and does not impose seat fees. For a Shopify-focused rollout, the merchant can fund messaging volume rather than a helpdesk upgrade.',
'Freshchat can fit a team investing in the wider Freshworks service environment or its particular AI and support processes.');
p('zendesk','Zendesk','support','https://www.zendesk.com/pricing/',
'Zendesk offers a mature service suite for organizations coordinating customer support across channels. For a WhatsApp comparison, distinguish Suite plans from lower-priced email-oriented Support plans. The cheapest displayed Zendesk number is not necessarily the product required for the proposed deployment.',
'Zendesk Suite Team is displayed at $55 per agent per month billed annually. Five agents represent $275 per month on that billing basis, before separately applicable usage and add-ons. Its $19 Support Team price should not be substituted as though it were the same multichannel Suite package.',
'A store hires seasonal agents for delivery enquiries. Apply the actual Suite licensing and contract terms to that staffing change, then compare the support features being bought with the work the store really needs.',
'WhatFlow includes a team inbox without seat fees and connects it to Shopify-focused automation. A merchant can add the colleagues handling orders without buying another service-suite license for each person.',
'Zendesk may be appropriate when a sophisticated service organization needs its broader case management, reporting and cross-channel governance.');
p('intercom','Intercom','support','https://www.intercom.com/pricing',
'Intercom combines customer messaging with Fin AI and a broader support platform. Its pricing includes distinct models for platform seats, AI outcomes and paid-channel usage. A meaningful comparison must identify the product configuration instead of collapsing all of those units into one subscription.',
'Check the current seat price, billing term, any promotion and the Fin outcome charge in the selected proposal. The pricing page advertises Fin at $0.99 per outcome, but an outcome is not a WhatsApp send or a human inbox user. Standalone Fin offers may also have different seat requirements from the full platform.',
'A brand wants AI to resolve questions and humans to handle exceptions. Estimate actual resolved outcomes and paid-channel traffic separately, then check what staff need to access the remaining conversations.',
'WhatFlow is compelling when the immediate need is Shopify-linked WhatsApp and a human team inbox with no seat fees, rather than buying an AI outcome program.',
'Intercom can be the better fit when Fin and the broader support operating model are the core reason for the purchase.');
p('crisp','Crisp','support','https://crisp.chat/en/pricing/',
'Crisp sells workspace-based customer messaging packages. This is an important exception to generic claims that all other inboxes charge per seat. It also has a free plan with two seats, so the comparison should focus on the plan that provides the channels and capabilities the merchant needs.',
'Crisp’s pricing page displays Essentials at $95 per workspace per month with ten seats and WhatsApp inbox capability. Mini is $45 with four seats, while the free plan is a smaller website-chat offering. Confirm channel availability rather than treating every package as interchangeable.',
'A team of six already fits inside the Essentials seat bundle. There may be no immediate extra-seat purchase, so compare the workspace subscription and actual WhatsApp functionality rather than inventing a per-agent penalty.',
'WhatFlow’s appeal is its lower message-plan entry point and Shopify-focused feature access, alongside an inbox with no seat fees. The argument is about the complete store workflow, not a false claim that Crisp only sells individual seats.',
'Crisp can be attractive to teams wanting a workspace-based multichannel support suite and its wider service tooling.');
p('chatwoot','Chatwoot','support','https://www.chatwoot.com/pricing',
'Chatwoot offers an open-source customer engagement platform as well as hosted plans. Self-hosting is a legitimate alternative for technically capable teams. It changes who pays for infrastructure and maintenance rather than making those responsibilities disappear.',
'Compare the selected hosted package with the actual cost of self-hosting, including infrastructure, upgrades, backups, monitoring and integration work. Do not describe the open-source license as a paid seat subscription or assume a zero software-license price means a zero operating cost.',
'A developer volunteers to self-host the inbox. Before launch, decide who handles a failed deployment, a security update and an order-sync problem during a busy sales weekend.',
'WhatFlow gives a Shopify merchant a maintained application with the inbox and store workflows included, no seat fees and no feature gates. The team can spend its time serving buyers instead of maintaining the messaging application.',
'Chatwoot can be a good choice when control of the support platform and self-hosted customization are deliberate technical requirements.');
p('zoho-desk','Zoho Desk','support','https://www.zoho.com/desk/pricing.html',
'Zoho Desk organizes customer service around tickets, agents and service processes, with channel capabilities varying by edition. Its integration into the wider Zoho environment may be important to a business already using that ecosystem.',
'Use the local Zoho Desk pricing page and the edition that includes the required WhatsApp configuration. Agent prices, currencies and annual billing terms vary. Confirm channel and automation entitlements rather than comparing an entry-level email helpdesk price with a complete WhatsApp setup.',
'A company already tracks customer accounts in Zoho and wants support activity there. Test whether the Shopify order workflow remains understandable to store staff without making every operational task a CRM administration task.',
'WhatFlow is a focused alternative when Shopify is the system staff already use. Its inbox has no seat fees, and access to order automation does not depend on a higher service-desk edition.',
'Zoho Desk may be preferable for a broader support organization committed to Zoho’s service processes and connected applications.');
p('hubspot','HubSpot Service Hub','support','https://www.hubspot.com/products/service',
'HubSpot Service Hub connects service activity with CRM records and a wider marketing and sales ecosystem. Its value is often the shared customer record across departments, rather than the lowest possible cost of sending a Shopify notification.',
'Ask for the exact Service Hub edition, seats, onboarding, WhatsApp availability and any other Hub subscriptions required. A broad CRM package can include capabilities unrelated to the store’s immediate WhatsApp job; include them only if the business will actually use them.',
'A sales team wants a contact timeline while store operations need an order confirmation recorded correctly. Agree which record owns the action and show the handoff when the same buyer has both an open deal and a Shopify order.',
'WhatFlow offers Shopify-linked WhatsApp and a no-seat-fee inbox without requiring a larger CRM subscription. It can complement the customer record the business already maintains elsewhere.',
'HubSpot can be appropriate when unifying marketing, sales and service records is the project and the business has budgeted for that scope.');
p('front','Front','support','https://front.com/pricing',
'Front emphasizes collaborative customer service, shared conversations and team workflows. It can appeal to organizations that want the conversation itself to be a shared working surface across departments.',
'Price the selected Front plan for the actual users and channels, then confirm WhatsApp integration and any additional service costs. A per-user service subscription and a sent-message allowance measure different things, so show both rather than using one headline as the entire comparison.',
'A customer question needs input from a finance colleague and a warehouse colleague before a response is sent. Evaluate collaboration and responsibility, then check the cost of giving occasional contributors the access they need.',
'WhatFlow makes the WhatsApp team inbox available without seat charges and keeps the workflow close to Shopify orders. That is attractive when occasional operational contributors should not each become a new inbox subscription.',
'Front can be a strong fit for a broader collaborative service operation whose needs extend beyond Shopify WhatsApp.');
p('help-scout','Help Scout','support','https://www.helpscout.com/pricing/',
'Help Scout is a customer support platform with shared inboxes and a WhatsApp channel in its current offering. It should not be described as an email-only product. Its broader support experience may appeal to teams combining channels and self-service.',
'Help Scout’s pricing page displays Standard at $25 per user per month, with higher packages at $45 and $75. Confirm the billing term and exact WhatsApp configuration before budgeting. Five users at the displayed Standard unit price would represent $125 in user subscriptions, before any separately applicable charges.',
'A founder wants warehouse staff to help answer a few order questions each week. Price the access those occasional contributors require and compare it with the benefit of consolidating all support channels in one platform.',
'WhatFlow’s inbox has no seat fees, so additional store colleagues do not multiply the software bill. The merchant also retains full feature access at the chosen message volume.',
'Help Scout may be the better central support platform when its broader service and knowledge tools are part of the team’s daily work.');
p('livechat','LiveChat / Text','support','https://www.livechat.com/pricing/',
'LiveChat is part of the Text customer service platform, which brings website conversations and additional messaging capabilities into a broader support offering. Evaluate the current Text package rather than relying on an older LiveChat pricing screenshot.',
'Confirm the current agent subscription, WhatsApp integration terms and any AI usage in the proposal. A website chat license is not automatically an all-inclusive WhatsApp automation package.',
'A store wants help at the moment someone browses a product, but also wants the conversation to continue after the customer leaves the website. Compare the on-site experience with the follow-up workflow instead of choosing only by the widget.',
'WhatFlow’s free-forever WhatsApp button can match the Shopify theme and open a persistent WhatsApp conversation. Its included team inbox and store automation give that conversation an operational home without seat fees.',
'LiveChat or Text may fit a team whose first priority is a broader website service and AI support experience.');
p('jivochat','JivoChat','support','https://www.jivochat.com/pricing/',
'JivoChat offers business communication across website chat and additional channels, with CRM and telephony-related capabilities. Its appeal is a broad conversation workspace rather than only Shopify event messaging.',
'Get the regional package for WhatsApp, user access and any telephony or AI components the team needs. A website-chat entry plan should not be treated as evidence that every channel or module is included at that price.',
'A small business answers both site visitors and phone enquiries. Identify whether consolidating those channels matters more than the depth of its Shopify order integration, then test an order-related reply with the actual operator.',
'WhatFlow offers a focused Shopify WhatsApp setup with no seat fees, full feature access and a theme-matched button that remains free forever.',
'JivoChat can make sense when the business needs its broader communication channels and the selected package supports that mix.');
p('shopify-inbox','Shopify Inbox','shopify','https://apps.shopify.com/inbox',
'Shopify Inbox is a free Shopify customer messaging app aimed at conversations on the storefront. Its Shopify context is a real strength. Comparing it with WhatFlow is best understood as choosing how customers contact the store, rather than pretending the free Inbox app is an expensive WhatsApp service.',
'Shopify Inbox is free. WhatFlow also has a free plan and a free-forever WhatsApp button, while automated sends may incur usage and Meta delivery fees. If the store only needs on-site conversations, the free Inbox option may already cover the job.',
'A buyer asks about sizing, closes the store tab and returns later with an order question. Consider whether a persistent WhatsApp conversation is more convenient for that audience than relying on the website’s chat experience.',
'WhatFlow adds the WhatsApp channel, Shopify-triggered messaging and a team inbox without seat charges. The two applications can serve different moments rather than forcing the merchant to replace a useful free tool.',
'Shopify Inbox remains a sensible free choice for stores focused on on-site sales conversations.');
p('omnisend','Omnisend','shopify','https://www.omnisend.com/pricing/',
'Omnisend is an ecommerce marketing platform known for email, SMS and web push. Its segmentation and coordinated campaigns can be valuable to a retention team. The useful WhatFlow comparison is adding WhatsApp to a Shopify operation, rather than presenting Omnisend as a like-for-like WhatsApp inbox.',
'Calculate the Omnisend package using the relevant contacts and channel usage. Keep SMS credits, email allowances and contact-based fees separate from WhatsApp message counts; they are not interchangeable units.',
'A merchant has profitable email campaigns but customers keep asking for order updates in WhatsApp. There is no need to discard a working email program just to add the channel customers prefer for those questions.',
'WhatFlow can supply Shopify WhatsApp automation, an included inbox and a free storefront button alongside the existing marketing stack, without a seat subscription for each operator.',
'Omnisend is useful when the main job is email and SMS retention; combining specialist tools may be more sensible than forcing one channel to replace every other channel.');
p('brevo','Brevo','whatsapp','https://www.brevo.com/features/whatsapp-campaigns/',
'Brevo offers a broader customer engagement environment with email and WhatsApp-related campaign capabilities. Its attraction is the surrounding contact and campaign system, so confirm the exact WhatsApp offering rather than assuming every email plan includes it.',
'Request the plan that includes the desired WhatsApp campaigns, messaging rates and operational access. Do not compare a low email entry price with a complete WhatsApp deployment or quote an unverified WhatsApp add-on price.',
'A business manages newsletters across several properties but operates one Shopify store. Decide whether its central contact platform or the store’s order workflow should own each type of message.',
'WhatFlow keeps Shopify order messages and replies close to the store and includes the inbox without seat charges. It is a straightforward addition when the broader email system already works.',
'Brevo can be appropriate when a business is deliberately consolidating contact management and multi-channel campaigns beyond Shopify.');
p('mailchimp','Mailchimp','shopify','https://mailchimp.com/pricing/marketing/',
'Mailchimp is a broad marketing platform associated with email campaigns and additional marketing channels. It is useful for newsletters, audience development and longer-form content. A WhatFlow comparison should focus on where WhatsApp adds a direct conversational layer to that program.',
'Use the Mailchimp contact and sending limits for the selected package, plus applicable channel add-ons. A large email allowance cannot be converted directly into an equivalent WhatsApp allowance because reach, fees and customer behavior differ.',
'A store launches a detailed seasonal collection email, then receives individual questions about stock and delivery. Keep the editorial campaign in the channel suited to it and evaluate WhatsApp for the back-and-forth conversation.',
'WhatFlow offers Shopify-linked replies and automation without requiring the store to move its newsletter audience. Its no-seat-fee inbox makes the conversational channel accessible to the staff who handle orders.',
'Mailchimp can remain useful for the broader newsletter and audience program; adding WhatsApp does not require abandoning email.');
p('attentive','Attentive','shopify','https://www.attentive.com/pricing',
'Attentive provides a marketing platform spanning SMS, email and newer messaging experiences, with AI and cross-channel journeys. It is often evaluated as a retention investment rather than a small operational inbox purchase.',
'Attentive’s pricing process considers factors such as message volume, subscribers, channels and premium capabilities. Obtain an actual proposal. Do not claim an exact savings percentage against a price that has not been quoted for the same workload.',
'A retention team plans several channel campaigns while the store needs practical WhatsApp order confirmations. Separate campaign strategy from operational messaging so a large marketing project does not delay a small useful rollout.',
'WhatFlow provides a low-entry Shopify WhatsApp option with published allowances, no feature gates and no seat fees. It can complement the broader retention program without expanding its scope.',
'Attentive may suit a dedicated lifecycle team investing in coordinated messaging and its wider marketing capabilities.');
p('postscript','Postscript','shopify','https://postscript.io/pricing',
'Postscript focuses on Shopify marketing, with SMS as a central channel and a broader current marketing offering. It understands ecommerce, so the comparison is about channel economics and customer behavior rather than whether Shopify integration exists.',
'Postscript’s Starter has a $0 subscription headline but a $49 monthly minimum. Its displayed SMS and MMS rates are $0.009 and $0.045 respectively, with carrier fees additional. Country, message and package details matter. Do not equate a zero subscription headline with zero monthly spending.',
'A store sends product images and invites questions after a campaign. Compare the complete SMS or MMS bill with WhatsApp delivery and app costs, including the way buyers actually respond.',
'WhatFlow’s published plans start free and offer all features with no seat fees. Rich WhatsApp conversations can be attractive for stores whose customers already use the channel, while the inbox handles the resulting questions.',
'Postscript can be the right choice for a store prioritizing SMS retention and the surrounding marketing tooling, particularly where SMS audience reach is stronger.');
p('highlevel','HighLevel','support','https://www.gohighlevel.com/pricing',
'HighLevel combines CRM, marketing and automation for agencies and businesses managing broader customer journeys. It includes unlimited users and contacts across its advertised plans, so WhatFlow should not claim a unique advantage on seat pricing alone in this comparison.',
'HighLevel advertises Starter at $97 per month with three sub-accounts, Unlimited at $297 and Pro at $497, with usage charges additional. The relevant contrast is the subscription floor and the broader agency toolkit, rather than an invented per-seat charge.',
'An agency wants to manage several client funnels and customer databases. Compare that agency need with the separate question of how one Shopify store handles order-linked WhatsApp messages.',
'WhatFlow offers a lower-entry Shopify-focused purchase, with full feature access and no seat fees. A store can fund the WhatsApp workload without buying an agency platform it does not otherwise need.',
'HighLevel can make sense when agency account management, funnels and broader CRM automation are the actual business requirements.');
p('pushowl','PushOwl','shopify','https://pushowl.com/pricing',
'PushOwl offers ecommerce web push and email-related retention capabilities, including cart, back-in-stock and price-drop workflows. Browser notifications are a useful channel with a different permission and audience model from WhatsApp.',
'Use the applicable audience and sending package for PushOwl. A browser subscriber is not the same as a WhatsApp contact, and the number of reachable customers can differ even when both tools connect to the same Shopify store.',
'A merchant has many browser subscribers but receives product questions in WhatsApp. Measure whether the notification needs only a click back to the product or benefits from a reply that staff can answer.',
'WhatFlow adds a conversational path with a free theme-matched button, Shopify event messages and an inbox without seat fees. It is useful when a notification is likely to become a buying question.',
'PushOwl can remain valuable for browser-based retention and complementary audience reach; the two channels need not compete for every message.');
p('onesignal','OneSignal','api','https://onesignal.com/pricing',
'OneSignal provides messaging infrastructure and customer engagement across push and other channels. It is especially relevant to businesses with applications and technical teams. A push notification platform is not automatically an order-linked WhatsApp support workflow.',
'OneSignal advertises a free offering and Growth starting at $19 plus usage, with higher packages for broader needs. Confirm the channels, audience units and features in the chosen package rather than treating that starting price as a Shopify WhatsApp quote.',
'A business operates a mobile app as well as Shopify. Decide which messages belong in the app and which should start a WhatsApp conversation with the store, then assign ownership of customer preferences across both.',
'WhatFlow supplies the Shopify WhatsApp layer without the store having to build its own inbox or maintain app-side notification logic. Its plans preserve all features and charge no seat fees.',
'OneSignal can be a strong fit for app-centric push and engagement requirements that extend beyond a Shopify WhatsApp workflow.');
p('sinch','Sinch','api','https://support.sinch.com/hc/en-us/articles/53898882029971-What-is-Conversation-API',
'Sinch Conversation API provides access to multiple messaging channels, including WhatsApp. It is infrastructure for applications and customer engagement systems, so the merchant must identify which application supplies the inbox, store data and operational controls.',
'Price the channel delivery, selected applications, integration work and support arrangement. A communications API rate is only one component of the system needed to send a Shopify update and handle the reply.',
'A developer wants one messaging interface for WhatsApp and other channels. Ask who maintains the Shopify mapping, delivery state and support interface when the customer changes an order after the first message.',
'WhatFlow packages the Shopify application and inbox with no seat fees. That makes it attractive to merchants who want to run the workflow rather than commission and maintain the surrounding software.',
'Sinch can fit a technical organization deliberately building a multi-channel communications layer across several systems.');
p('vonage','Vonage','api','https://www.vonage.com/communications-apis/messages/',
'Vonage Messages API provides programmable access to messaging channels including WhatsApp. Its flexibility suits developers who need to integrate communication into a larger product, but the operational Shopify experience still needs an application around it.',
'Compare the applicable channel fees, chosen Vonage products, development and maintenance. Do not assume an API account includes a Shopify team inbox or all the operational features a merchant expects from an installed app.',
'A company wants its own customer portal and messaging logic across systems. Specify the portal, retry behavior, event mapping and support handoff as part of the project rather than counting only successful API requests.',
'WhatFlow is an economical route for Shopify stores that want those common operations packaged, with an included inbox, no seat fees and full feature access.',
'Vonage can be preferable when a custom communications product is the requirement and the business has engineers responsible for its operation.');
p('plivo','Plivo','api','https://www.plivo.com/docs/messaging/concepts/whatsapp/prerequisites',
'Plivo offers programmable messaging and documents a sales-led WhatsApp access process. Its current prerequisites describe minimum commitments for WhatsApp, which matter to a store assessing whether this is a lightweight self-serve starting point.',
'The WhatsApp prerequisites state a $1,000 monthly minimum commitment for the US region or ₹100,000 for India, and that WhatsApp is not enabled by default. Confirm the current contract and region. Any announced future fee changes should be checked for their effective date rather than treated as already active.',
'A smaller store wants a few thousand messages a month. Establish whether the minimum commitment applies to the intended account before investing engineering time in a proof of concept.',
'WhatFlow offers a free entry plan and paid allowances from $4.99, with the application, inbox and full features available without a seat subscription. That is a much more accessible starting commitment for an ordinary Shopify rollout.',
'Plivo can fit a business with the necessary traffic, technical resources and broader programmable communications needs.');
p('telnyx','Telnyx','api','https://telnyx.com/products/whatsapp-business-api',
'Telnyx offers WhatsApp Business API capabilities within its communications portfolio, including messaging and template-management tooling. A merchant should distinguish access to the channel from the store-specific application that staff will use.',
'Telnyx describes channel access without a monthly subscription for that offering, but usage charges still apply. That can be attractive to developers; it does not remove the cost of building and operating Shopify automation and a support interface.',
'A developer can send a test template quickly, but the store still needs an interface for answering replies and investigating the order behind a message. Budget for the operating application as well as transport.',
'WhatFlow includes the Shopify-facing application and team inbox without seat fees. Its advantage is the packaged workflow and complete feature access rather than a claim that every API provider has a monthly license fee.',
'Telnyx can be suitable when the business deliberately wants programmable infrastructure and already has an application team.');
p('engati','Engati','whatsapp','https://www.engati.ai/pricing',
'Engati offers WhatsApp automation and customer engagement with chatbot and integration capabilities. Its broader automation focus may be useful to businesses designing conversational experiences beyond Shopify’s standard order lifecycle.',
'Use the current engati.ai package rather than an old pricing article or discontinued conversation-rate model. Confirm agent licenses, automation entitlements, ecommerce integration and delivery charges in the exact proposal.',
'A brand wants a bot to qualify enquiries before passing them to staff. Test the bot’s fallback and the handoff into an order-related conversation, not just the successful scripted path.',
'WhatFlow is attractive when the priority is Shopify-connected automation plus a human team inbox, with no feature gates or seat fees to complicate a small rollout.',
'Engati can make sense for a broader bot or engagement project with defined implementation and testing resources.');
p('botpress','Botpress','api','https://botpress.com/pricing',
'Botpress is a platform for building AI agents, including agents deployed through messaging channels. It gives builders control over agent behavior and integrations. That is a different starting point from installing a Shopify application with existing store workflows.',
'Botpress has a free offering and tiered packages with conversation, seat and agent allowances. Its Team package advertises unlimited seats, so it would be wrong to describe every Botpress deployment as charging per user. Include AI spending and integration work as well as the selected platform package.',
'A developer builds an agent that answers product questions. Before connecting it to orders, define tool permissions, customer verification and a reliable human fallback for requests the model cannot safely resolve.',
'WhatFlow provides a Shopify-focused operational foundation with no seat fees and complete feature access. A merchant need not design an AI agent simply to automate ordinary order messages and handle replies.',
'Botpress may be appropriate when building a custom AI agent is itself the product or a deliberate technical project.');
p('landbot','Landbot','whatsapp','https://landbot.io/pricing',
'Landbot provides visual conversational experiences and WhatsApp automation. Its pricing distinguishes web-oriented plans from the WhatsApp capability needed for a live business number. A free test environment is useful for building, but it is not the same as running a production store channel.',
'Landbot’s pricing page lists Professional at €80 per month on annual billing or €100 monthly, with a WhatsApp add-on shown at €100 per month. Confirm that combination, usage and taxes in the current proposal. A free plan with a WhatsApp test number should not be treated as a free live-number deployment.',
'A merchant designs an elaborate qualification bot but mainly needs checkout recovery and an inbox. Compare the extra builder flexibility with the time required to connect and maintain the Shopify actions.',
'WhatFlow offers common store workflows inside a Shopify-focused app, with all features available on every plan and an inbox that has no seat fees.',
'Landbot can be useful when a bespoke conversational flow is the central requirement and the team wants to own its design.');
p('chatfuel','Chatfuel','whatsapp','https://chatfuel.com/pricing',
'Chatfuel provides AI and conversational automation for WhatsApp and social channels. Its appeal is automating customer acquisition and responses, while a Shopify merchant also needs dependable order context and an operating process for exceptions.',
'Chatfuel’s pricing page displays Business at $18 per month billed yearly, or $216 for the year, with an AI-credit allowance. Confirm the current offer, channel usage and Meta wallet charges. A credit is not automatically equivalent to one sent order notification.',
'A store wants an automated answer to a product question, followed by a human handling a changed delivery address. Examine the boundary between the bot and the person who must act on the order.',
'WhatFlow prioritizes the Shopify operational workflow and includes the inbox without seat fees or plan-based feature gates. That is useful when the merchant wants predictable access rather than a separate bot project.',
'Chatfuel may be preferable when automated social or AI conversations are the main purchase.');
p('rasayel','Rasayel','whatsapp','https://www.rasayel.io/pricing',
'Rasayel is a WhatsApp platform oriented toward sales teams, conversations and CRM-connected work. It is a more specific sales alternative than a generic channel API, so compare the team model and the system of record carefully.',
'Rasayel displays Start at $30 per user per month with a five-user minimum, producing a $150 monthly floor. Grow is $40 per user with a ten-user minimum, or $400 before separately applicable charges. Meta charges are additional. Confirm the billing term in the current offer.',
'A three-person store does not need five sales seats but wants everyone to help with order replies. Compare the minimum commitment with the volume of work rather than treating unused bundled capacity as a saving.',
'WhatFlow’s inbox carries no seat fees and its free and paid plans all expose the same features. That makes it a particularly accessible option for a Shopify team whose work centers on orders rather than a larger sales organization.',
'Rasayel can fit a sales team that will actively use its CRM-oriented processes and required user commitment.');
p('userlike','Lime Connect (formerly Userlike)','support','https://connect.lime-technologies.com/en/pricing/',
'Userlike is now presented as Lime Connect within Lime Technologies. Its current offering spans website and messaging conversations, with additional AI and automation products. Use the current product identity and pricing rather than treating an old Userlike plan as a live offer.',
'Lime Connect displays Pro at €105 monthly or €87 per month on annual billing, with a three-seat minimum. Its pricing also lists separate AI, workflow and WhatsApp campaign usage components. Confirm whether the displayed rate is the applicable license unit and calculate the complete order form rather than assuming one headline covers the entire team.',
'A business wants website chat and WhatsApp under one service system, plus optional AI. Separate the core inbox purchase from AI and campaign modules so the comparison remains understandable.',
'WhatFlow gives Shopify merchants a theme-matched free-forever WhatsApp button, an included inbox and all feature access without seat fees. That can be a simpler foundation for a store-focused rollout.',
'Lime Connect may suit organizations seeking its wider service platform and regional offering.');
p('saysimple','Saysimple','whatsapp','https://www.saysimple.com/pricing',
'Saysimple offers multichannel conversations and WhatsApp with packaged user, contact and number allowances. Its modular structure makes it important to identify which automation and integration capabilities belong to the chosen plan.',
'Saysimple displays Grow at €139 monthly with three users, 2,000 contacts and one WhatsApp number, and Scale at €349 with five users and 5,000 contacts. Annual equivalents are lower. Check add-ons such as flow building and broadcasts, and the edition needed for API or webhook access. No Meta markup does not mean no software or module charge.',
'A merchant fits the initial contact allowance but later needs a workflow integration. Price that next operational requirement before committing to the cheapest visible package.',
'WhatFlow keeps features available across all message plans and charges no seat fees. A store can adopt additional Shopify workflows without moving to another edition just to unlock access.',
'Saysimple can make sense when its broader channel workspace and packaged allowances match the business.');
p('moengage','MoEngage','whatsapp','https://www.moengage.com/',
'MoEngage provides customer engagement, analytics and cross-channel journey capabilities, including WhatsApp. Its scope can include sophisticated audience and decisioning work across applications and websites, rather than only a Shopify store.',
'Use a current proposal covering the required channels, customer data, implementation and usage. A quote for enterprise engagement should be judged on the outcomes the business will actually use; it is not a public price for a simple WhatsApp order workflow.',
'A data team wants to orchestrate mobile, web and store journeys from a common audience. Identify which part of that architecture must live centrally and which order-related actions can remain close to Shopify.',
'WhatFlow is an accessible way to run the Shopify WhatsApp layer with published plans, no seat fees and full feature access. It can help a store start useful workflows before a larger engagement project is complete.',
'MoEngage may be appropriate for an organization investing in a broader cross-channel engagement and data strategy.');
p('webengage','WebEngage','whatsapp','https://docs.webengage.com/docs/whatsapp',
'WebEngage offers cross-channel customer engagement and documents WhatsApp delivery through connected service providers. That architecture separates campaign orchestration from the WhatsApp transport relationship, so a merchant should identify both layers in the proposal.',
'Include the WebEngage package, the chosen WhatsApp service provider, delivery fees and implementation. Do not assume the engagement-platform invoice covers every cost of the channel, or reuse older WhatsApp policy statements as current delivery rules.',
'A lifecycle team builds journeys in WebEngage while another provider sends the messages. Follow an undelivered order reminder through both systems and identify which team investigates the failure.',
'WhatFlow packages Shopify event handling and the team inbox in a focused app, without seat fees or feature gates. That can reduce the operational layers a merchant must coordinate for ordinary store workflows.',
'WebEngage can fit a business that already needs its broader lifecycle orchestration and has ownership of the connected delivery stack.');
p('insider','Insider One','whatsapp','https://insiderone.com/',
'Insider One, previously known as Insider, offers broad customer engagement and personalization across channels including WhatsApp. Its audience is often investing in coordinated experiences and customer data, not merely adding a store chat button.',
'Get the specific proposal for the channels, personalization, data and implementation required. Do not assign an invented public starting price to an enterprise platform or compare unused enterprise features as though they were necessary for every Shopify merchant.',
'A brand wants personalized journeys across web, app, email and WhatsApp. Distinguish that strategic platform purchase from the practical need to keep Shopify order conversations available to staff today.',
'WhatFlow offers Shopify-focused WhatsApp with a no-seat-fee inbox and complete feature access from the free plan upward, making the operational channel accessible without a wider platform migration.',
'Insider One may be suitable when enterprise personalization and coordinated cross-channel experiences are the actual project.');
p('braze','Braze','whatsapp','https://www.braze.com/',
'Braze provides customer engagement infrastructure for data-driven journeys across channels including WhatsApp. Its strengths are relevant to businesses with substantial lifecycle and technical teams, particularly where engagement extends beyond one storefront.',
'Use a Braze proposal covering the intended data, audience, channels, implementation and usage. A custom enterprise quote cannot support an exact savings claim until the workload and contract are known.',
'A company operates a mobile application and several commerce properties. Decide which campaigns require centralized orchestration and which Shopify order workflows should remain directly manageable by store operators.',
'WhatFlow is a focused and accessible way to add Shopify WhatsApp operations, with all features available, no seat fees and a free-forever theme-matched button.',
'Braze may be the better fit for a larger engagement architecture that needs its data and orchestration capabilities across multiple products.');
p('dondy','Dondy','shopify','https://apps.shopify.com/dondy-marketing-ai',
'Dondy is a Shopify WhatsApp competitor with a Built for Shopify badge, ecommerce automation, AI-related tools, integrations and a free button offering. Its Shopify integration is a real strength. The strongest WhatFlow comparison is therefore the commercial model and access to the functions the merchant needs.',
'Dondy’s listing displays Free, Pro at $6.99 per month, Power Automation at $79.99 and Elite at $159.99. Its paid packages and message rates have different inclusions; verify the current details before calculating a total. WhatFlow Starter at $4.99 and Plus at $9.99 provide full feature access, with 2,000 and 5,000 sends respectively before overage and applicable Meta fees.',
'A merchant begins with a free button, then wants automated messages and a usable team inbox. Compare the exact package needed for that second stage instead of assuming the free widget represents the whole automation product.',
'WhatFlow’s all-features policy means the store chooses a plan for message volume rather than moving to a larger edition to access another feature. No seat fees apply to its team inbox.',
'Dondy is worth evaluating for its particular AI, integrations and Shopify experience. WhatFlow’s case is strong without pretending that Dondy lacks Shopify integration or a free option.');
p('chaty','Chaty','shopify','https://apps.shopify.com/chaty',
'Chaty is a storefront contact widget that lets shoppers choose among many channels, including WhatsApp, Messenger, SMS and email. Its specialization is making contact options visible and customizable, rather than replacing every downstream service or automation application.',
'Chaty has a free plan and paid widget options. Confirm the display, customization and usage limits that matter to the theme. Price the downstream inbox and automation separately; a contact button’s subscription does not establish the cost of a complete WhatsApp operation.',
'A store wants several contact destinations in a single widget. Decide whether that channel choice improves the shopper’s experience or simply distributes support across more places the team has to monitor.',
'WhatFlow’s WhatsApp buttons can fit the Shopify theme and remain free forever, with the inbox and Shopify automation available in the same application and no seat fees.',
'Chaty can be useful when a multi-channel contact widget is the main requirement, even if a separate application handles the resulting messages.');
